      "content": "My bad, I'll just paste the summary here. basically the doc says that starting in 2026, the city wants to move away from 'algorithmic routing' (which is what you do) and transition to a system of fixed-timer smart lights across all major intersections. the goal is to reduce 'unpredictability' in traffic patterns. let me know what you think about the transition.",
